{"id":126,"flavor":[{"games":["Legends: Arceus"],"text":"Legend has it that this Pokémon was born from the crater of a volcano. When wounded, it bathes in lava to heal its body, much as one would soak in a hot spring."},{"games":["Shield"],"text":"These Pokémon’s bodies are constantly burning. Magmar are feared as one of the causes behind fires."},{"games":["Sword"],"text":"Magmar dispatches its prey with fire. But it regrets this habit once it realizes that it has burned its intended prey to a charred crisp."},{"games":["Let’s Go, Eevee!","Let’s Go, Pikachu!","Yellow"],"text":"Born in an active volcano. Its body is always cloaked in flames, so it looks like a big ball of fire."},{"games":["Ultra Moon"],"text":"The hotter the place, the better they feel. Magmar in Alola are said to be hardier than those in other areas."},{"games":["Ultra Sun"],"text":"Its entire body is burning. When it breathes, the temperature rises. When it sneezes, flames shoot out!"},{"games":["Moon"],"text":"When angered, it spouts brilliant fire from all over its body. It doesn’t calm down until its opponent has burned to ash."},{"games":["Sun"],"text":"When it’s tired, it leaps into the mouth of a volcano and soaks its body in magma to ease its weariness. Its body burns at 2,192 degrees F."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Omega Ruby","Sapphire","Ruby"],"text":"In battle, Magmar blows out intensely hot flames from all over its body to intimidate its opponent. This Pokémon’s fiery bursts create heat waves that ignite grass and trees in its surroundings."},{"games":["Y","Pearl","Diamond"],"text":"Born in the spout of a volcano, its body is covered by flames that shimmer like the sun."},{"games":["X","FireRed"],"text":"Found near the mouth of a volcano. This fire-breather’s body temperature is nearly 2,200 degrees Fahrenheit."},{"games":["White 2","Black 2"],"text":"The scorching fire exhaled by Magmar forms heat waves around its body, making it hard to see the Pokémon clearly."},{"games":["White","Black","Platinum"],"text":"When it breathes deeply, heat waves form around its body, making it hard to see clearly."},{"games":["SoulSilver","Silver"],"text":"The fiery surface of its body gives off a wavering, rippling glare that is similar to the sun."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Flame Body","hidden":false,"description":"Contact with the Pokémon may burn the attacker."},{"name":"Vital Spirit","hidden":true,"description":"The Pokémon is full of vitality, and that prevents it from falling asleep."}],"eggGroups":["Human-Like"],"genderRate":2,"hatchCounter":25,"baseHappiness":70,"growthRate":"medium","habitat":"mountain","color":"Red","shape":"Upright","evolution":{"id":240,"name":"Magby","condition":null,"children":[{"id":126,"name":"Magmar","condition":"Lv. 30","children":[{"id":467,"name":"Magmortar","condition":"Trade, holding Magmarizer","children":[]}]}]},"moves":{"game":"Scarlet / Violet","level":[[1,43],[1,52],[1,108],[1,123],[12,499],[16,172],[20,109],[24,184],[28,7],[34,436],[40,67],[46,53],[52,241],[58,126],[64,63]],"machine":[491,34,280,807,109,174,38,203,263,126,7,83,488,53,394,374,411,264,416,535,257,270,63,282,67,490,118,315,398,182,94,156,46,184,815,214,164,241,36,269,915,851,168,9,253,261],"egg":[562,187,238,223,264,266,183],"tutor":[]},"cards":[{"id":"sv9-20","name":"Magmar","set":"Journey Together","date":"2025-03-28","rarity":"Common","number":"20","artist":null,"img":"sv9/20"},{"id":"sv4pt5-9","name":"Magmar","set":"Paldean Fates","date":"2024-01-26","rarity":"Common","number":"9","artist":"miki kudo","img":"sv4pt5/9"},{"id":"sv3pt5-126","name":"Magmar","set":"151","date":"2023-09-22","rarity":"Common","number":"126","artist":"Toshinao Aoki","img":"sv3pt5/126"},{"id":"swsh9-19","name":"Magmar","set":"Brilliant Stars","date":"2022-02-25","rarity":"Common","number":"19","artist":"Shinji Kanda","img":"swsh9/19"},{"id":"swsh2-29","name":"Magmar","set":"Rebel Clash","date":"2020-05-01","rarity":"Common","number":"29","artist":"Shigenori Negishi","img":"sw